<title>CANADA: Suncor raises Canada posted oil prices.</title>
<headline>Suncor raises Canada posted oil prices.</headline>
<dateline>CALGARY 1997-07-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Suncor Energy Inc said on Wednesday it raised the price it would pay for Edmonton light sweet crude oil by C$4.00/cubic metre or C$0.64/barrel, to C$172.00/cubic metre or C$27.35/barrel, effective immediately.</p>
<p>Other prices were listed as follows:</p>
<p>Cromer light sour C$164.00/cubic metre, or C$26.07/barrel</p>
<p>Midale at Cromer C$148.00/cubic metre, or C$23.53/barrel</p>
<p>((Reuters Calgary Bureau (403) 531-1624))</p>
</text>
